What:           /sys/class/sec/tsp/dt2w_timeout
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        HTML6405
Description:
                Maximum double-tap-to-wake window in seconds on battery
                after display powerdown or external power disconnect. Accepts
                decimal values from 0 through 86400.
                The default is 300 (five minutes); 0 means unlimited. Changes
                apply on the next display powerdown or external power
                disconnect and do not restart an active window. dt2w_enable
                must also be enabled.

                External USB, AC or dock power pauses the timeout, including
                when the battery is full. Disconnecting external power starts
                a fresh window. Connecting it after timeout powers the touch
                controller back on and reactivates DT2W while dt2w_enable is
                enabled, without requiring display resume.

                For example, 300 allows double-tap wake for five minutes on
                battery, and indefinitely while externally powered.
                At expiry, the driver restores the saved touch configuration,
                disables the touch IRQ, powers off the controller and releases
                its suspend blocker. Full system suspend is then permitted;
                other wake locks may still prevent it. Use the power button
                or another supported wake source after expiry. Display resume
                powers the controller back on; the next display powerdown
                starts a new window.

                On this board the touch interrupt uses a normal GPIO, so
                full system suspend is blocked while gesture wake is active.
                This setting does not make that interrupt wake-capable.
